    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4184" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁλι-εύω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅλς</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fish,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ev.Jo.
				21.3
			</span></i>; <i>to be a fisher</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				29
			</span></i>; <i>fish for, catch</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπάρους</span> dub. l. in <i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				54
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίθους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Pisc.</u>
					47
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Herm.</u>
				65
			</span></i>, etc.: metaph. of avenger, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁλιεύειν τινάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Je.</u>
					16.16
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> only 
				Med.
			 occurs in 
				Att.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.Com.
				44
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἁλιευομένη</span>, title of
			play by <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
			</span></i>:—also later, <i><span class="en">
				Posidon.
				68
			</span></i>.</div>
